    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b9ad3e14216c2f08",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "a5cead3bd84d7a88b05ecf648794dc1d7374bb5d55693a2d584171bb997d1d86",
      "text": "Day 6 · Breakfast. Excursion to the Argentine side of the falls, across the Tancredo Neves Bridge over the Iguazu River. In a 55,500-hectare national park, walkways take you close to and even directly beneath the falls, to see the birth of the waterfalls and the famous Devil’s Throat, the largest of all, and to admire them from viewing platforms high above. Then transfer to the airport for your flight to Buenos Aires, where a driver meets you for the transfer to the hotel.",
